{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Circle.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Circle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"magic circle magic circle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Circle.md","fileName":"Magic Circle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Magic Circle","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Player Experience Design]] · [[Game Definition and Forms]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Player Experience Design","Game Definition and Forms","Game Rule","Metagaming","Pretending","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Circle.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Circle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"magic circle magic circle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Circle.md","fileName":"Magic Circle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Magic Circle","heading":"Magic Circle","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The magic circle is the conceptual boundary that separates play from ordinary activity. Inside it, the game's own [[Game Rule|rules]], meanings, goals, and consequences organize what actions count.\n\nThe boundary can be porous: [[Metagaming]] may carry information, relationships, or consequences across individual sessions and beyond the immediate play context. Even so, the game remains an arbiter of the shared state within the circle.\n\nEntering the magic circle means agreeing to [[Pretending|pretend]] and to treat the game's rules and symbols as meaningful. An action that is pointless or unacceptable in ordinary life can acquire a clear purpose inside this consensual context.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Player Experience Design","Game Definition and Forms","Game Rule","Metagaming","Pretending","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Circle.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Circle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"magic circle magic circle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Magic Circle.md","fileName":"Magic Circle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Magic Circle","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n\n[[fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Player Experience Design","Game Definition and Forms","Game Rule","Metagaming","Pretending","advancedgamedesign.pdf","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}